# 📚 Linked List (Part 5) - Circular Linked List

## 📌 Introduction

A **Circular Linked List (CLL)** is a variation of the Linked List where the **last node points back to the first node (Head)** instead of pointing to `NULL`.

This creates a circular structure, allowing continuous traversal without reaching the end of the list.

Circular Linked Lists are widely used in:

- Round Robin Scheduling
- Multiplayer Games
- Music & Video Playlists
- CPU Scheduling
- Circular Queues
- Token Ring Networks

