# 8️⃣ Circular Linked List vs Singly Linked List

| Feature | Singly LL | Circular LL |
|----------|-----------|-------------|
| Last Node | Points to NULL | Points to Head |
| Traversal | Ends at NULL | Ends at Head |
| Continuous Traversal | ❌ | ✅ |
| Memory | Same | Same |
| Implementation | Easier | Slightly Complex |

---

# 9️⃣ Advantages

✅ Continuous traversal

✅ No NULL pointer at the end

✅ Efficient implementation of Circular Queues

✅ Useful in Round Robin Scheduling

✅ Easy cycling through elements

---

# 🔟 Disadvantages

❌ Traversal is more complex

❌ Risk of infinite loops

❌ More difficult debugging

❌ Extra care required while updating pointers

