# 💡 Interview Tips

✅ The last node always points to the Head.

✅ Use a **do-while loop** for traversal.

✅ Always stop traversal when you return to the Head.

✅ Handle the single-node list separately.

---

# ⚠️ Common Mistakes

❌ Infinite loops during traversal.

❌ Forgetting to reconnect the last node.

❌ Losing the Head pointer.

❌ Incorrect handling of one-node lists.

---

# 📝 Summary

- A Circular Linked List has no NULL at the end.
- The last node points back to the Head.
- Traversal stops when the Head is reached again.
- It is useful in scheduling, circular queues, and playlists.
- Special care is required to avoid infinite loops.

